<title>USA: GM poised to idle more U.S. workers -UAW.</title>
<headline>GM poised to idle more U.S. workers -UAW.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp is poised to idle several hundred more workers at its Ypsilanti, Mich., transmission plant starting at the end of third-shift production on Tuesday if the GM Canada strike is not resolved, union officials said.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for United Auto Workers Local 735 said GM notified the union that third shift workers on one of the plant's product lines are tentatively scheduled to not report to work on Wednesday, while first and second shift employees on the same product line will be idled after their Wednesday shifts are complete.</p>
</text>
